course: dictionary
lesson: 2641
title: Words for people who are held
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A detainee is a person who is kept in a prison, or held by the police or the army. Detain means to hold someone and keep them from leaving. The word is formal, so you will meet it mostly in news, history and law.
explain: Read the clue words in the dictionary sentence: «"Detainee" means a prisoner, often held without trial (never judged in a court).» Prisoner tells you the person is locked up. Held tells you someone is keeping them. Without trial tells you the court has not judged them yet.
explain: Swap your meaning into a sentence to check it. «The detainee waited in a small room at the police station.» If detainee means a person held by the police and not yet judged, the sentence makes sense. If you had guessed a visitor or a guard, it would not.
fact: A detainee is a person who is held, often in prison, by the police or the army.
fact: «Detainee» means a prisoner, often held without trial.
fact: Detain comes from a word meaning to hold back or keep someone somewhere.
fact: «Prisoner» is a close synonym, but detainee is a more formal word that often means a person not yet judged in a court.
fact: Clue words such as held, prisoner and without trial help you work out a hard word from its context.
exercise: «"Detainee" means a prisoner, often held without trial.» What does detainee mean? | A teacher who marks homework | *A person who is held, often without trial yet | A person who wins a prize | A judge who decides a case in court
exercise: Which clue word in «a prisoner, often held without trial» tells you the person has not yet been judged? | *trial | often | prisoner | held
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to detainee? | gardener | *prisoner | teacher | judge
test: «The detainees were kept in the camp until their case was checked.» What does detainees mean here? | Guards who keep the gates | Visitors who bring presents | Children on a school trip | *People being held, not free to leave
test: Which word is the best synonym for detainee in a news report about a police station? | Gardener | Shopper | Teacher | *Prisoner
exam: Which is the best meaning of detainee? | *A person held in prison or by police or army, often without trial yet | A person who writes the news | A person who is free to go wherever they like | A person who is always late for school
